WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.237
This example uses LAG to compare an admission with the previous discharge for the same subject.

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:10.672
The logic is the same kind of sequence analysis we used earlier.

00:00:10.672 --> 00:00:14.927
In Spark, this window query may require sorting within each subject partition.

00:00:14.927 --> 00:00:17.902
Run the query and inspect the gap column.

00:00:17.902 --> 00:00:25.797
Window functions work in Spark SQL much like in PostgreSQL, but they can require sorting and shuffling within

00:00:25.797 --> 00:00:26.292
partitions.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:32.637
Define the business partition and sequence carefully, then inspect the physical plan when the dataset is

00:00:32.637 --> 00:00:36.960
large. Correct logic comes first; distributed cost comes next.
